            b) Plant : <Abstract >
This defines the basic properties and methods for any plant life in the world
                • Properties :
                    ◦ edible <bool> : determines if a creature can eat this plant
                    ◦ currentCalories <num> : The amount of calories available for any creature to who consumes it
                    ◦ maxCalories <num> : The maximum amount of calories available for this plant
                    ◦ growthRate <num> : the number of calories that get restored per game day, up to the value of maxCalories.
                    ◦ size <num> : the area in square feet this plant takes up.
                    ◦ seedSpread <num>: the area in feed from the center of this plant that a seed can take root away from this plant
                    ◦ seedRate <num> : number of game days that it takes for the plant to spread seeds
                    ◦ seedCalReq <num> : the minimum number of callories required on the day the seed is spread that are required for the seed to be released
                    ◦ seedChokeRake <num> : the rate at which this plant’s seeds will replace any plants already in place
                    ◦ movementImpact <num> : the % reduction in speed for a creature passing through
                    ◦ fitSize <num> : if the size of the creature < this value, the creature can move through at normal speed.
                    ◦ crushWeight <num> : The weight at which a creature passing through will destroy this object
                • Methods :
                    ◦ spreadSeed(spread, currCals, reqCals) <internal> : 
			
This function is called by the concrete Plan object when it is time to spread seeds. It first checks to see if the currCals value is >= reqCals. If not it returns. If so it checks the spread distance, generating a random distance and direction where the distance is < spread feet from this plant object.

            c) Environment : <Abstract>
This defines the properties and methods for all environmental objects such as stone, dirt, or water.
                • Properties :
                    ◦ passible <bool> : If false, this is a solid object that creatures can not pass through
                    ◦ movementImpact <num> : the % reduction in speed for a creature passing through
                    ◦ fitSize <num> : if the size of the creature < this value, the creature can move through at normal speed.
                    ◦ crushWeight <num> : The weight at which a creature passing through will destroy this object. 0 means it’s unbreakable
