            a) statToPoint(statNum:int) <function> This function takes the input and compares it against an array or calculates if it exceeds the precalculated values.
                • Logic:
statList <num list> = [132.82, 158.62, 187.29, 219.15, 254.54, 293.87, 337.56, 386.11, 440.06, 500.00, 559.94, 613.89, 662.44, 706.13, 745.46, 780.85, 812.71, 841.38, 867.18, 890.40, 911.30, 930.11, 947.04, 962.28, 975.99 ]
if statNum> 25
{
currPoints <num> = 975.99
modifier <num> = 13.71
diff <int> :  statNum – 25

for (diff > 0;  --diff)  {currPoints = currPoints + (modifier *.9) and modifier = modifier – (modifier * .1)}}
}
else{ currPoints  = statList[statNum -1]}
return  currPoints
